---
import AtlasExplorer from '../components/AtlasExplorer.tsx';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A source-conscious atlas for reading the Mahabharata as a web of choices, vows and consequences."
    />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#172016" />
    <title>Itihāsa Atlas — Mahābhārata</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <section class="opening" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <header class="masthead">
          <a class="wordmark" href="#top" aria-label="Itihasa Atlas home">
            ITIHĀSA
            <span>ATLAS</span>
          </a>
          <p class="masthead__edition">MĀHĀBHĀRATA / READING OFFICE</p>
          <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
            <a href="#atlas">ATLAS</a>
            <a href="/verse-lens">VERSE LENS</a>
            <a href="/pathfinder">PATHFINDER</a>
            <a href="/protocol">PROTOCOL</a>
          </nav>
        </header>

        <div class="opening__grid">
          <div class="opening__copy">
            <p class="label label--sage">SABHĀ PARVA / ENTRY POINT 01</p>
            <h1 id="hero-title">
              The dice were
              <br />
              never only
              <br />
              <em>a game.</em>
            </h1>
            <p class="opening__dek">
              A reading instrument for the promises, silences and legal questions that
              make the Mahābhārata impossible to flatten into a single story.
            </p>
            <a class="enter-link" href="#atlas">
              TRACE THE PRESSURE <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            </a>
          </div>

          <aside class="case-sheet" aria-label="The dice hall reading prompt">
            <div class="case-sheet__topline">
              <span>READING PROMPT</span>
              <span>01 / 11</span>
            </div>
            <pre aria-hidden="true">┌──────────────────────────┐
│       SABHĀ  HALL         │
│                          │
│  YUDHIṢṬHIRA ── WAGER     │
│        │                 │
│        └──── DRAUPADĪ ?   │
│                          │
│  THE COURT DOES NOT ANSWER│
└──────────────────────────┘</pre>
            <p class="case-sheet__question">
              When a king loses himself, what exactly is left for him to stake?
            </p>
            <div class="case-sheet__source">
              <span>BASE TEXT</span>
              <strong>CRITICAL EDITION</strong>
              <span>STATUS</span>
              <strong>EDITORIAL DRAFT</strong>
            </div>
            <a href="#atlas">OPEN THIS QUESTION ↘</a>
          </aside>
        </div>

        <footer class="opening__footer">
          <span>START AT THE DICE HALL</span>
          <span>FOLLOW THE CONSEQUENCE, NOT THE CHARACTER</span>
          <span>EDITION-AWARE / REVIEW-GATED</span>
        </footer>
      </section>

      <AtlasExplorer client:load />

      <section class="protocol" id="protocol" aria-labelledby="protocol-title">
        <p class="label">READING PROTOCOL</p>
        <div class="protocol__number">02</div>
        <div>
          <h2 id="protocol-title">
            No node is
            <br />a final answer.
          </h2>
          <p>
            Every record keeps its attestation visible. The Critical Edition is the
            working baseline; received and regional traditions are named where they change
            the story.
          </p>
        </div>
        <small>
          Sanskrit text, transliteration and translation stay marked as draft until a
          named reviewer checks them. This interface makes that limit visible instead of
          hiding it in a footnote.
        </small>
        <a class="protocol__link" href="/protocol">
          READ THE FULL PROTOCOL ↗
        </a>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
